  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CTP&apos;s contribution towards the purchase of solar batteries to Catholic University of South Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The Juba Campus started in 2008 with 30 students and at present counts around 2.600 students (44% women), pursuing BA and Diplomas in the Faculties of Economics and Business Administration, Education, Environmental Sciences and in the Institute of Peace and Conflict Studies.

In 2016 the campus purchased a system of 150 solar panels and 24 industrial solar batteries to provide power to 12 classrooms plus offices. From 2020 the system has alimented also the 36 desktops of the Computer Lab and, from 2023, the 15 desktops of the ICT Centre. The extreme heat of February-March 2024 affected the already dated batteries, and from November 2024 the stand-by generator had to replace the solar system with high fuel expenses and increased air and acoustic pollution.
The university is seeking for funds from its partners and well-wishers to replace the expired batteries and buy new ones to ease the high operational costs of fuel and the generator.</narrative>
  </description>
